%% A signature type from the exposed module's own scope chain.  -expose lifts
%% the exported procedures of lib/inner/rates.glp "(and the types their
%% signatures carry) into that directory's scope, as if defined in its
%% self.glp" (TGLP modules.tex, "The -expose directive"), and "a declaration
%% carries the transitive closure of the types its signature references"
%% (modules.tex, "Procedure declarations").  rate/2's signature names Level,
%% which lib/self.glp defines: Level is in the scope of rates.glp
%% (Definition (Root, Scope)) and not in this one, so the lift reads the
%% signature in the scope of rates.glp and carries Level here.  This layer
%% exports nothing and is not a program; app/ is, and lib/self.glp is not on
%% its chain, as social/graph/self.glp is not on sglp's when the root self.glp
%% exposes social#graph#routing#intro.
-expose(lib#inner#rates).
